# Architecture & Implementation Report: Unified Tab-Route Relative & Member Creation Workflow

## 1. Executive Summary & Objective

### User Request:
> *"but thsi ceate page will be under tah route noe fully sepate page as id show active route"*

### Meaning & Goal:
1. The relative / member creation view must reside **directly under the active tab route** (e.g., `/user-dashboard?tab=members&action=create` or `/user-dashboard?tab=tree&action=create`), rather than navigating away to a detached URL route.
2. The **active sidebar navigation item** (e.g. **"Family Directory"** or **"Family Tree"**) must stay actively highlighted and glowing while creating a relative.
3. The create interface remains a **full-width, dedicated form view** (not a cramped modal pop-up), while existing strictly under the dashboard's tab routing architecture.
4. Clean back navigation and form cancellation seamlessly restore the default tab view (`/user-dashboard?tab=members` or `/user-dashboard?tab=tree`).

---

## 2. Component & Routing Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                SanctuaryDashboardWrapper                                    │
│  - Sidebar: "Family Directory" [ACTIVE - purple highlight]                                   │
│  - URL: /user-dashboard?tab=members&action=create                                           │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                               │
                                               ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                            UserDashboardContent (Tab Switcher)                              │
│                                                                                             │
│  switch (currentTab) {                                                                      │
│    case "members":                                                                          │
│      if (action === "create") {                                                             │
│        return <CreateMemberForm role="MEMBER" />;  <-- FULL FORM VIEW (NOT A MODAL)         │
│      }                                                                                      │
│      return <MembersTab role="MEMBER" />;                                                   │
│                                                                                             │
│    case "tree":                                                                             │
│      if (action === "create") {                                                             │
│        return <CreateMemberForm role="MEMBER" />;  <-- FULL FORM VIEW (NOT A MODAL)         │
│      }                                                                                      │
│      return <TreeTab role="MEMBER" />;                                                      │
│  }                                                                                          │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## 3. Implementation Details

### 3.1 Active Route Preservation in Sidebar (`SanctuaryDashboardWrapper.tsx`)
The `isActive` logic in the sidebar was upgraded so that any sub-routes, actions, or tab queries keep their parent sidebar link highlighted:

```typescript
const isActive = isOwnerOrAdmin
  ? (pathname === "/owner-dashboard" && currentTab === item.tabKey) ||
    pathname === `/owner-dashboard/${item.tabKey}` ||
    pathname.startsWith(`/owner-dashboard/${item.tabKey}/`)
  : (pathname === "/user-dashboard" && currentTab === item.tabKey) ||
    (pathname === "/user-dashboard" && !searchParams?.get("tab") && item.tabKey === "dashboard") ||
    pathname === item.href ||
    pathname === `/user-dashboard/${item.tabKey}` ||
    pathname.startsWith(`/user-dashboard/${item.tabKey}/`);
```

### 3.2 Tab-Level Conditional Rendering (`user-dashboard/page.tsx` & `owner-dashboard/page.tsx`)
Inside the dashboard tab switchers, when `searchParams?.get("action") === "create"`:
- Under `case "members"`: Renders `<CreateMemberForm role="..." />`.
- Under `case "tree"`: Renders `<CreateMemberForm role="..." />`.
- The user is NOT presented with a modal; they see the full-page form directly within the dashboard tab workspace.

### 3.3 Trigger Buttons (`MembersTab.tsx` & `TreeTab.tsx`)
- Clicking **"Add Relative"** / **"Add Family Member"** in `MembersTab`:
  - Navigates to `/user-dashboard?tab=members&action=create` (or `/owner-dashboard?tab=members&action=create`).
- Clicking **"Add Relative"** in `TreeTab`:
  - Navigates to `/user-dashboard?tab=tree&action=create&relativeTo=...&relativeToName=...`.
- The active sidebar route stays **100% active and highlighted**.

### 3.4 Deep-Link Forwarding (`user-dashboard/members/create/page.tsx`)
If a user directly visits or bookmarks `/user-dashboard/members/create` or `/user-dashboard/relatives/create`, the page automatically forwards to `/user-dashboard?tab=members&action=create`, ensuring the active sidebar tab and unified layout are always preserved.

---

## 4. Verification Matrix

| Action | Route | Sidebar Active Tab | View Rendered |
| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |
| Click "Add Relative" from Directory | `/user-dashboard?tab=members&action=create` | **Family Directory** | Full Create Form (No Modal) |
| Click "Add Relative" from Tree | `/user-dashboard?tab=tree&action=create` | **Family Tree** | Full Create Form (No Modal) |
| Click "Cancel" or "Back" | `/user-dashboard?tab=members` (or `tree`) | Preserved | Returns to directory/tree view |
| Direct hit to `/members/create` | Forwards to `?tab=members&action=create` | **Family Directory** | Full Create Form (No Modal) |
